Z||000000||Tweek||06-24-2001||07:16 AM||||Im willing to bet that many of us have little questions about our cars that could be very easily answered by someone with that working part...  for example I remember someone who didn't know that the car came equipped with a blue dingy thingy...  anyways..  I've got 4 ques..<P>1. Up with the map lights, I have 3 buttons. The two on either side turns the lights on. I suspect that the middle one has to do with the doors opening, as my lights have never come one with the doors opening.<P>2. What is the rectangualr space right above the tach used for, you can see it here:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.oswg.net/Ted/Misc/dash0002.jpg"> <P>3. On the 84 only models I think, what do the right vent and left vent pull handles do?<P>4. Are the winshield wipers supposed to "park" like in every other GM car?<P>Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||06-24-2001||07:53 AM||||Well I'll answer what I can.<P>1. I have seen the 3-button ones but don't know what it's for. Why not just open the door and push the button?<P>2. The space on the dash is just there. I think it's for if the dash was a right-hand drive you could swap the odometer/speedo with the tach. Afriend found a cheap green LED clock at a flea market once and installed the clock there. It looked neat but too bright at night. Maybe an LCD could be put there?<P>3. They open and close the vent door for outside air.<P>4. If by "park" you mean do they stop at the low point then move down a little more when turning off, then no they don't.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodrv6||06-24-2001||08:41 AM||||I have 3 buttons on the light console on my 84.  The outer ones turn on the outer lights on the console.  The middle one turns on all the interior lights that normally come on when a door is opened.  It's kind of redundant since you can do the same thing by rolling the thumbwheel under the headlight switch all the way up. I've noticed that my 88 only has the two outer switches.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Rodrv6 (edited 06-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tweek||06-24-2001||08:50 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Rodrv6:<BR><B>I have 3 buttons on the light console on my 84.  The outer ones turn on the outer lights on the console.  The middle one turns on all the interior lights that normally come on when a door is opened.  It's kind of redundant since you can do the same thing by rolling the thumbwheel under the headlight switch all the way up. I've noticed that my 88 only has the two outer switches.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hmm...  thats weird, cause pressing that button and rolling up the thumbwheel do absolutly nothing for me...||||reg||1
Z||000004||84 2in1||06-24-2001||11:55 AM||||On my 84 the bulbs were blown in the light fixture and they were missing by the kick panals. You know tht the fuse is good because the other reading/map lights work. hope it helped-B-||||reg||1
